{"date": "2026-10-28", "word": "Flat", "summary": "A flat day (forecast flat). Thermals stayed flat all day. The upslope ran from about 08:30 to about 17:45. A low day for October: the base stayed down near 3,000 ft (normal 4,500\u20135,400 ft). The evening before, the page called it normal, about 3,900 ft, a miss. Midday the base averaged about 3,000 ft by the Kekoa camera, 900 ft lower than the evening's number; the morning update said about 3,800 ft, off by 800 ft. Most of the day the shear line was at Pukalani; furthest south about 16:22, crossing Kula Highway between Pukalani and Kamehameha Schools. Data gaps: no readings all day from 1 station (Nakula); Upper Kahikinui stopped at 13:50; Kahikinui stopped at 13:55; the Mesonet could not be reached on 16 of 53 updates.", "therm": "<strong>Flat</strong> for the day, 10:00\u201314:00<div class=\"sub\">Kula Ag's measured air through the NAM sounding (thermal.py); forecast was Flat</div>", "base": "", "notes": ["Saturated, dew-fed morning: low cloud until about 08:45.", "Base held flat at about 3,000 ft from 08:30 for about 6 hours.", "Watched for: Base will lift (P3) from 08:37; Late-day decay (P7) from 17:07."], "chart": "<div class=\"watch\"><div class=\"kind\">What the day did</div><ul><li>Saturated, dew-fed morning: low cloud until about 08:45.</li><li>Base held flat at about 3,000 ft from 08:30 for about 6 hours.</li><li>Watched for: Base will lift (P3) from 08:37; Late-day decay (P7) from 17:07.</li></ul></div><div style=\"font-weight:600;font-size:.9rem;margin:10px 0 2px\">Cloudbase, derived</div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:.8rem;color:var(--muted,#6b6b66);margin:2px 0 4px\">\n\n<span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:16px;height:2px;background:#2a78d6;vertical-align:middle\"></span> Derived (stations)</span><span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:#3f9d5a;vertical-align:middle\"></span> Kekoa camera</span></div>\n<div s